# What a group's header's OWN code is held to: the diagnostics of the region
# its include stands in (design.md §4.19, §1.12; panel 205's R2, ratified
# 2026-10-10; defect 569).
#
# **A header's own code was judged by where it was found.** clang quiets
# every warning located in a header it finds in a system directory, whatever
# `-I` says (GCC's and clang's documentation), so on Linux arm64 `gmp.h` in
# `/usr/include` built and printed `6`, while on this Mac the same program,
# `gmp.h` found under Homebrew through pkg-config's `-I`, was refused by
# `-Werror=sign-conversion` at `gmp.h:1882`, inside the library's own inline
# code, before any binding was checked; libavutil, avcodec, avformat,
# swscale and libfdt alike. And an environment variable decided it on one
# machine: `CPATH` refused it, `C_INCLUDE_PATH` (a system directory to
# clang) built it.
#
# **So the region is judged as one policy, wherever the header was found**:
# the diagnostic state is pushed, `-Wall` and `-Wsign-conversion` are
# ignored, the two families a library's own style trips, and the warnings
# that say the header's code the program RUNS has no defined behaviour, a
# missing return, a read of an uninitialised value, stay errors (`KEPT`, which
# `-Wall`'s ignore would otherwise take); `-Wshorten-64-to-32`, the pointer
# types and clang's default errors are not in `-Wall` and stay as the build's
# flags set them. The region is popped at the guard's close, and every check
# of a binding is raised again after it (`emit/checks_raised.hero`, defect
# 570), so nothing a header's code is excused from reaches a line the
# compiler wrote. Measured at the landing, 2026-10-10: the six libraries
# build on this Mac, `CPATH` and `C_INCLUDE_PATH` agree, a header of the
# program's own with a missing return, an uninitialised read or a 64-to-32
# narrowing is refused; panel 204's 182 Mac headers read 10 refusals and 0
# raw warnings where they read 16 and 2, exactly the six moving, and the 85
# Linux arm64 headers copied to a directory of the user's 2 where they read
# 3, `gmp.h` moving; and of the 1,456 tracked files with an `extern`, no
# program moved but the defect's own cases.

use emit/checks_raised

# What a header's own code is not held to.
constant QUIETED: [str]
    [
        "-Wall"
        "-Wsign-conversion"
    ]

# What it still is, which `-Wall`'s ignore would otherwise turn off: each an
# error on the build's command line too (`cli/flags.hero`).
constant KEPT: [str]
    [
        "-Wreturn-type"
        "-Wuninitialized"
        "-Wconditional-uninitialized"
    ]

# The lines before the groups' includes: the push, the ignores, the kept.
function opening() -> [str]
    out: [str] @ ["#pragma clang diagnostic push"]

    for word in QUIETED
        out @ out.push("#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"" + word + "\"")

    for word in KEPT
        out @ out.push("#pragma clang diagnostic error \"" + word + "\"")

    return out

# The line after the guard's close, which gives back the state before the
# region; a header's own push left open is what the checks raised after it
# answer.
constant CLOSING: str
    "#pragma clang diagnostic pop"

## Tests

test "a header's own code is quiet of -Wall and sign conversion alone, a missing return and an uninitialised read kept"
    got = opening()
    assert got[0] == "#pragma clang diagnostic push"
    assert got[1] == "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wall\""
    assert got[2] == "#pragma clang diagnostic ignored \"-Wsign-conversion\""
    assert got[3] == "#pragma clang diagnostic error \"-Wreturn-type\""
    assert got.len() == 1 + QUIETED.len() + KEPT.len()

    # Each kept warning is a check the build raises after the region too.
    for word in KEPT
        found: bool @ false

        for one in checks_raised.checked()
            if one == word
                found @ true

        assert found
